{"user": "If I play g2 now (flips f2,g3,g4,g5,g6 - 5 discs), does that let White grab h1 corner next turn and end up worse for me overall, compared to playing b6 or a7 instead?", "user_ts": "2026-08-11T23:37:02.027745+00:00", "assistant": "Yes \u2014 **g2 lets White take h1**: after **g2**, the diagonal **h1\u2013g2\u2013f3** makes **h1** legal for White. That corner is permanent, so your 5-disc grab can backfire.\n\nBetween the alternatives, **a7 is best for the final count** here. It doesn\u2019t open **h1**, and the lower-left edge is already influenced by White\u2019s **a8** corner, so it\u2019s the least costly way to play.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-11T23:37:02.027745+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-11T23:37:07.027745+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Think Aloud", "Common Ground Question"], "consensus": ["Think Aloud", "Common Ground Question"], "votes": {"Think Aloud": 2, "Common Ground Question": 3}, "confidence": {"Think Aloud": 0.6666666666666666, "Common Ground Question": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Think Aloud", "Common Ground Question"], "llama": ["Think Aloud", "Common Ground Question"], "sonnet": ["Common Ground Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Move Verdict", "Local Justification", "Worked Line", "General Principle"], "consensus": ["Move Verdict", "Local Justification", "Worked Line", "General Principle"], "votes": {"Move Verdict": 3, "Local Justification": 3, "Worked Line": 3, "General Principle": 2, "Paraphrase": 1, "Neutral Feedback": 1, "Positive Feedback": 1}, "confidence": {"Move Verdict": 1.0, "Local Justification": 1.0, "Worked Line": 1.0, "General Principle": 0.6666666666666666, "Paraphrase": 0.3333333333333333, "Neutral Feedback": 0.3333333333333333, "Positive Feedback": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Move Verdict", "Local Justification", "Worked Line", "General Principle", "Paraphrase", "Neutra