{"user": "Looking back - when I played a3 and White had to pass, was that the key moment that turned the game around for me? I want to understand why that worked.", "user_ts": "2026-08-11T23:37:17.027745+00:00", "assistant": "Yes \u2014 **that was probably the key turning point**.\n\nWhy **a3** worked:\n\n- It **forced White to pass**, meaning White had *zero legal moves*.\n- A forced pass is huge in the endgame: you effectively get **two Black moves in a row**.\n- It\u2019s not about how many discs a3 flipped immediately; it was about **mobility** \u2014 you took away White\u2019s replies.\n- That let you control the remaining sequence instead of letting White choose the best corner/edge timing.\n- Final result here is **Black 33, White 31**, so that tempo swing likely made the difference.\n\nRule reminder: if a player has no legal move, they **must pass**; if both players have no move or the board is full, the game ends.", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-11T23:37:17.027745+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-11T23:37:22.027745+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Knowledge Deficit Question", "Common Ground Question"], "consensus": ["Knowledge Deficit Question", "Common Ground Question"], "votes": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 3, "Common Ground Question": 3}, "confidence": {"Knowledge Deficit Question": 1.0, "Common Ground Question": 1.0}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Knowledge Deficit Question", "Common Ground Question"], "llama": ["Knowledge Deficit Question", "Common Ground Question"], "sonnet": ["Knowledge Deficit Question", "Common Ground Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle", "Positive Feedback"], "consensus": ["Board Report", "Local Justification", "General Principle", "Positive Feedback"], "votes": {"Local Justification": 3, "General Principle": 3, "Positive Feedback": 2, "Board Report": 2}, 