{"user": "After White passed, I played g2 next (flipping 5), then White took h1 (flipping g2 back), then I was forced into a1. Was that the best possible order for me, or did I get lucky that it still worked out to a win?", "user_ts": "2026-08-11T23:37:32.027745+00:00", "assistant": "It **still worked**, but **g2 was not the cleanest order**.\n\nAfter White passed, the stronger idea was likely:\n\n1. **a1 first** \u2014 flips b2 and **does not give White h1**\n2. White still has no move / very limited mobility\n3. Then Black can often take **h1** or **g2** in the best order\n\nBy playing **g2 first**, you opened the diagonal **h1\u2013g2\u2013f3**, so White got the **h1 corner**. You still won **33\u201331**, but that was a narrow win after giving White a permanent corner.\n\nKey lesson: after forcing a pass, don\u2019t automatically take the big flip. Ask: **Can I use the extra tempo to take or prevent a corner first?**", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-11T23:37:32.027745+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-11T23:37:37.027745+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Think Aloud", "Common Ground Question"], "consensus": ["Think Aloud", "Common Ground Question"], "votes": {"Think Aloud": 3, "Solution Request": 1, "Common Ground Question": 2}, "confidence": {"Think Aloud": 1.0, "Solution Request": 0.3333333333333333, "Common Ground Question": 0.6666666666666666}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Think Aloud", "Solution Request"], "llama": ["Think Aloud", "Common Ground Question"], "sonnet": ["Think Aloud", "Common Ground Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Local Justification", "Worked Line", "General Principle", "Neutral Feedback"], "consensus": ["Local Justification", "Worked Line", "General Principle", "Neutral Feedback"], "votes": {"Local Justification": 3, "Worked Line": 3, "General Principle": 3, "Neutral Feedback": 3, "Move Verdict": 1, "Board Report": 1, "Pro